62-67  USED by/SHARED with the stokes add-on

Coefficients 68 - 70 only apply if coefficients%i(73) = 1
---------------------------------------------------------

68  Determine how the local modulus is evaluated
    0: modulus is constant and determined in the standard way
    1: modulus is given by a function of position (coefficients%func1(1)%p
       where funcnr=md, where md is the mode number)
    2: modulus is given by nodal values (given in oldvectors%v1(md)%p(1),
       where md is the mode number)
    3: modulus is given in integration points (given in the 1d real vector with
       index md in oldvectors%e(1)%p, where md is the mode number)

69  Determine how the local relaxation time is evaluated
    0: relaxation time is constant and determined in the standard way
    1: relaxation time is given by a function of position
       (coefficients%func1(2)%p where funcnr=md, where md is the mode number)
    2: relaxation time is given by nodal values (given in
       oldvectors%v1(md)%p(2), where md is the mode number)
    3: relaxation time is given in integration points (given in the
       1d real vector with index md in oldvectors%e(2)%p, where md is the
       mode number)

70  Determine how the local non-linear parameters are evaluated
    0: non-linear parameters are constant and determined in the standard way
    1: non-linear parameters are given by a function of position
       (coefficients%func1(2+j)%p where funcnr=md, where md is the
       mode number and j is the index of the non-linear parameter)
    2: non-linear parameters are given by nodal values (given in
       oldvectors%v1(md)%p(2+j), where md is the mode number and j is the index
       of the non-linear parameter)
    3: non-linear parameters are given in integration points (given in the
       1d real vector with index md in oldvectors%e(2+j)%p, where md is the
       mode number and j is the index of the non-linear parameter)

71  Use the b-formulation:
    0: no
    1: contravariant deformation tensor (CDT)
    2: symmetric, i.e. b=sqrt(c)
    3: Cholesky
    4: Cholesky with log diagonals
    Note, that the b-formulation and log-conformation transformation
    (coefficients%i(21)=1) cannot be used at the same time.

72  A least square projection of c=b.b^T has been performed.
