75-77  USED by/SHARED with the stokes add-on

78  Check for zero velocity and use htype=3 and Uscaling=4 instead in SUPG.
      0: no
      1: yes
    If a zero velocity is detected in ANY of the integration points of an
    element, the method is switched to htype=3 and Uscaling=4 for ALL
    integration points.
    NOTE: this is a brute force approach to avoid divide by zero, when
          the velocity is exactly zero. It should be used only for that case
          and normally be off.
    NOTE: Uglobal = coefficient%r(10) must be set to a positive value.

79  how cn is computed in the integration points for stress-implicit methods
         0: take default value (=1)
         1: from nodal point value interpolation.
         2: directly in the integration points from c=exp(s) or c=b.b^T.
    Notes:
      a. This is only relevant if either the log-conformation has been set
         (coefficients%i(21)=1) or the use of the b-tensor formulation
         tensor has been set (coefficients%i(71)>=1). If not, both 1 and 2
         should give the same result.
      b. This does not affect the value of gradcn, which is always computed
         from nodal values of cn.
      c. A value of 2, garantuees positivity of the c-tensor in the integration
         points for the LCR of CDT method and stress-implicit schemes.
      d. The value of coefficients%i(79) does not affect the
         temporary ALE scheme (coefficients%i(48)=2), which still uses the
         scheme with value=1.

