82  USED by/SHARED with the stokes add-on

83  physqc: start of the physical quantities for the conformation. The actual
    physical quantity numbers for each of the modes is given by the array
       [ ( i, i=physqc,physqc+nmodes-1 ) ]
    This only applies when all the conformation modes are part of the system
    vector.

84  Storage in the system vector of the conformation for reading in
    element routines:
    0: The default for that routine. It depends on the typical usage. For
       example rhs_divtau will typically be used together with system vectors
       where each tensor component is stored in a separate sysvector.
    1: Each component is stored in a separate sysvector.
    2: Each mode is stored in a separate sysvector.
    3: All modes are stored in a single sysvector. physqc=coefficients%i(83) is
       used to separate the modes.
    NOTE: some routines force the storage for some vectors and the value
          of coefficients%i(84) is ignored for that vector. For example,
          reading projected conformation requires the storage format to be
          equal to 1 (each component in a separate system vector).

85  Mode number for specifying just a single mode.
    NOTE: overrides mode1/mode2 given by coefficients%i(26-27)) only if
          applicable and coefficient%i(85)>0. Only applicable to a few
          routines that set singlemode=.true. in the call to
          set_viscoelastic_elem (or directly to set_globals_viscoelastic).
          Other routines are unaffected by the value of coefficient%i(85).

86  The sysvector number for the velocity vector used for the SUPG weighting
    function:
    0: default = 1
    >0: the sysvector number
    This is currently only used in order to make the weighting function
    not dependent on the iteration solution for the velocity in the case
    of full Newton-Raphson.

87  The sysvector number for the iteration solution of the conformation tensor
    0: default. The default depends on the routine:
          implicit_divtau, implicit_ce_vel_supg_elem: 1
          implicit_ce_supg_elem: 3
       The reason for the different defaults is compatibility.
    >0: the sysvector number
    This is currently only used for the implicit routines.

88  The sysvector number for the conformation tensor at previous time step tn.
    0: default. The default depends on the routine:
